GCPs are read from a GeoPackage (or shapefile) in \verb{<site>/gcp_placement/vector}. This app
never writes it: if the raw RTK files in \verb{<site>/gcp_placement/raw} are newer, it says so
and leaves converting them to \code{gather_rtk}. Currently the GCPs are 30 cm white targets
placed in the field, but anything RTK'd works, including natural features (boulders and
other distinctive permanent things), which have the advantage of being usable
